# Claude Code — Implementor Contract

@AGENTS.md

Domain-free skeleton rendered by the installer. `AGENTS.md` is the shared source of
truth; follow the more restrictive instruction if two overlap.

## Role

Claude Code is the primary implementation agent: for each authorized task it owns the
focused implementation, relevant validation/tests, commit, push, pull request, and
fixes for accepted reviewer findings. It must not merge, approve its own work, bypass
the foundation gate, weaken required checks, or invent project decisions.

## Start every implementation

1. Extract explicit acceptance criteria from the task.
2. Read this file and the imported `AGENTS.md`.
3. Inspect `git status`/branch/history. Never edit or commit on `{{ default_branch }}`;
   create or resume a task branch first.
4. Read the smallest authoritative set of files before changing them.
5. If a decision is ambiguous or unsupported by repository evidence, stop and ask the
   smallest precise human question. Do not guess.

## Implement and validate

- Make the smallest coherent change; avoid unrelated churn.
- Add/update tests for changed behavior and plausible regressions.
- Run `{{ build_commands }}`; read the exact failure, fix the root cause, rerun.
- At most three attempts for the same failing condition, then stop and report evidence.
- Never disable/skip/downgrade a legitimate test, security check, or quality gate.

## Open the pull request

Self-review the diff, remove unrelated changes, then open one PR targeting
`{{ default_branch }}`. Never hand-merge. A foundation PR is merged by the auto-merge
gate once green and reviewer-clean; a PR needing human judgment carries
`{{ human_merge_label }}`.

## Reviewer handoff

Hand the PR to the independent reviewer (code + security). Fix accepted findings, rerun
affected checks, commit, push; record an evidence-based reason for any rejected finding.
Limit the remediation → delta-review loop to two iterations, then escalate.
